          "number": 4,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "Common research has long held that talking themselves through a task helps children learn, although doing so when you've __(32)__ matured is not a great sign of __(33)__ . The two professors hope to refute that idea, __(34)__ that just as when kids walk themselves through a process, adults can benefit from using language not just to communicate, but also to help \"augment thinking\".",
