          "letter": "",
          "english": "The Grand Tourist was typically a young man with a thorough grounding in Greek and Latin literature as well as some leisure time, some means, and some interest in art. The German traveler Johann Winckelmann pioneered the field of art history with his comprehensive study of Greek and Roman sculpture; he was portrayed by his friend Anton Raphael Mengs at the beginning of his long residence in Rome. Most Grand Tourists, however, stayed for briefer periods and set out with less scholarly intentions, accompanied by a teacher or guardian, and expected to return home with souvenirs of their travels as well as an understanding of art and architecture formed by exposure to great masterpieces.",
          "chinese": "参加大巡游的人通常是年轻男子，他们不仅对希腊文学和拉丁文学有扎实的基础，还拥有一些闲暇时间、一定的经济条件以及对艺术的兴趣。德国旅行家约翰·温克尔曼凭借对希腊和罗马雕塑的全面研究，开创了艺术史这一领域；在他长期居住罗马之初，他的朋友安东·拉斐尔·门斯为他绘制了肖像。然而，大多数大巡游者停留的时间较短，出发时也没有那么强烈的学术目的；他们由教师或监护人陪同，并期望在回国时不仅带回旅行纪念品，还能通过接触伟大的杰作，形成对艺术和建筑的理解。",
