          "number": 3,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "London was a frequent starting point for Grand Tourists, and Paris a compulsory destination; many traveled to the Netherlands, some to Switzerland and Germany, and a very few adventurers to Spain, Greece, or Turkey. The essential place to visit, however, was Italy. The British traveler Charles Thompson spoke for many Grand Tourists when in 1744 he described himself as \"being impatiently desirous of viewing a country so famous in history, a country which once gave laws to the world, and which is at present the greatest school of music and painting, contains the noblest productions of sculpture and architecture, and is filled with cabinets of rarities, and collections of all kinds of historical relics\". Within Italy, the great focus was Rome, whose ancient ruins and more recent achievements were shown to every Grand Tourist. Panini's Ancient Rome and Modern Rome represent the sights most prized, including celebrated Greco-Roman statues and views of famous ruins, fountains, and churches. Since there were few museums anywhere in Europe before the close of the eighteenth century, Grand Tourists often saw paintings and sculptures by gaining admission to private collections, and many were eager to acquire examples of Greco-Roman and Italian art for their own collections. In England, where architecture was increasingly seen as an aristocratic pursuit, noblemen often applied what they learned from the villas of Palladio in the Veneto and the evocative(唤起回忆的) ruins of Rome to their own country houses and gardens.",
          "chinese": "伦敦是大巡游者经常选择的出发地，而巴黎则是必到之地；许多人还前往荷兰，有些人去了瑞士和德国，极少数冒险者则前往西班牙、希腊或土耳其。不过，最不可或缺的游览地还是意大利。1744年，英国旅行家查尔斯·汤普森道出了许多大巡游者的心声，他形容自己“急切地渴望参观这样一个在历史上声名显赫的国家；这个国家曾经为世界制定法律，而如今是音乐和绘画领域最伟大的学校，拥有最崇高的雕塑和建筑作品，并收藏着珍奇物品陈列以及各种历史遗物”。在意大利境内，重点是罗马，那里古老的遗迹和较为近代的成就都会展示给每一位大巡游者。帕尼尼的《古罗马》和《现代罗马》描绘了最受珍视的景观，其中包括著名的希腊罗马雕像，以及著名遗迹、喷泉和教堂的景致。由于在18世纪末以前，欧洲各地几乎没有博物馆，大巡游者常常通过获准进入私人收藏来观赏绘画和雕塑，许多人还渴望为自己的收藏购得希腊罗马艺术和意大利艺术的作品。在英国，建筑越来越被视为贵族所从事的事业，贵族们常常把自己从威尼托地区帕拉迪奥的别墅和罗马那些令人联想起往昔的废墟中学到的东西，运用到自己的乡间宅邸和花园中。",
